.venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.egg-info/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Everything under data/ is runtime state, and this repository is public.
#
# Deny-by-default, not a list of known-bad paths. The list version of this file
# enumerated tenders.db, docs/, html/, captcha/ and secrets/ — and silently did
# not cover data/backups/, which holds *complete copies of the database*,
# including the push_subscriptions table (real subscriber endpoints, i.e. other
# people's personal data). 2.5 GB of it was staged and ready to be pushed to a
# public repo. Enumerating what to hide fails the moment a new directory
# appears; enumerating what to *keep* fails safe instead.
#
# Nothing in data/ belongs in git: config.ensure_dirs() recreates the tree, and
# the archive itself is rebuilt by scraping. If something here ever does need
# tracking, add a targeted `!data/thing` exception below and say why.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
data/

# The push identity. Called out separately from the blanket rule above because
# it is the one file whose exposure cannot be undone by deleting a commit: it
# is the credential that lets a server push notifications to every subscriber's
# device, and rotating it invalidates every existing subscription.
data/secrets/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Internal deployment runbook — not published.
#
# ARCHITECTURE.md documents *this specific installation*: the production
# server's IP address, home-directory paths, the hostname, the uid the units
# run under, and the username of a second person who works on the wider
# cluster. None of that helps anyone self-host their own mirror, and one of the
# names in it is not even ours to publish. The public equivalent is README.md
# plus docs/SELF-HOSTING.md, which describe the system without describing the
# machine it happens to run on.
#
# If a design-rationale document is ever wanted in the repo, write it fresh
# rather than scrubbing this one — a redaction pass over a runbook is exactly
# the kind of thing that misses a line.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
ARCHITECTURE.md

# Local tooling config, not project code. settings.local.json in particular
# accumulates absolute paths from whatever machine it was used on — this one
# had a personal Downloads path in it — and the ".local." in the name says it
# was never meant to be shared.
.claude/

# Obsolete macOS launchd agent with a hardcoded personal path baked into it
# (/Users/<someone>/Desktop/...). Superseded by deploy/*.service, which use
# systemd's %h so they work for whoever installs them.
scripts/com.tenders.forward.plist
